P3 stateful corners (P3_state, P3_state_k8) DEFERRED behind P4 — 04/08/2026, Luiz's order.

REASON: cost, measured not estimated. At sn=8 a NEURONS GENERATION costs ~4.6h (16657s
for gen 1 on the first attempt), ~150x the sn=0 arms' ~110s/gen. With patience-3 early
stop landing near gen 7-8 and a 120-gen MEMORY stage behind it, each of the 6 cells is a
multi-DAY run. P4's 6 cells are ~1.1h each, ~7h total, so running P4 first returns the
QUAD+E/I answer the same day instead of a fortnight from now.

NOT cancelled — deferred. Nothing about the design changed: 2 corners x 3 seeds on
dfa1l's actual sn recipe (--grid-state-neurons 8 12 16 --max-state-neurons 24,
--grid-bits 24 30, on=64, BINARY, L3D, pidmix nf=15), scored against A4's already-
measured stateless floor, with round 1 (both corners at s31337002) as the gate.

No stateful cell has a marker, so all 6 remain re-runnable. Relaunch with:
